        "reading_checked": "If a budget approval requires full-quarter coverage or evidence that advertising caused sales changes, a scatterplot limited by its title to selected high-growth quarters and lacking causal controls is insufficient; the evidence-review option is then appropriate.",
        "evidence": "The condition is a logical dependency: 'If standards require X, then Y is appropriate.' The chart evidence confirms the premise of the condition: the data is limited to 'Selected High-Growth Quarters' (title) and lacks causal controls (O3). Therefore, the reading correctly identifies that if the decision standard is strict (requiring full coverage/causality), the chart is insufficient. This is a valid applicability test based on the visible limitations of the data.",
        "status": "supported"
      }
    },
