          "evidence": "The points Q2, Q3, Q4, Q5, Q6 form a line rising from the bottom-left (approx 30, 63) to the top-right (approx 70, 168). Q6 is to the right and above Q5. Q5 is to the right and above Q4.",
          "status": "supported"
        }
      },
      "B": {
        "reading_checked": "If the horizontal axis encodes advertising spend and the vertical axis encodes sales, as their printed labels state, then points farther right and higher represent quarters with greater plotted spend and sales. If this selected-quarter association is considered sufficient and generalizable evidence for a broader budget change, it supports approving an ad-budget increase; the chart alone does not establish causation or represent all quarters.",
        "evidence": "The reading correctly interprets the axes (O2, O3) and the visual trend (O4). It correctly identifies the logical condition: if the association is deemed sufficient, it supports the 'Approve' option. It also correctly notes the limitation that the chart alone does not prove causation or represent all quarters (consistent with O1 and O3). This is a valid applicability test.",
